cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Ounce-Core in research or write about it, please cite it as below."
title: "Ounce-Core"
abstract: >-
  A safe-Rust AArch64 execution and verification lab. It runs ARM64 programs on three CPU
  engines (an interpreter, a block JIT, and native execution) and compares each result
  against real Apple Silicon hardware, so failures can be explained and passes can be shown
  with evidence.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Ounce-Core contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hffgzktbcc-blip/ounce-core"
url: "https://hffgzktbcc-blip.github.io/ounce-core/"
license: MIT
version: 0.6.1
date-released: "2026-11-09"
keywords:
  - aarch64
  - arm64
  - differential testing
  - emulation
  - verification
  - Rust
